82:- **C1 Rule tables and categoriser** (src/cma/categorise.py; rule tables as data under src/cma/rules/). Built-in tables v1 (today's) and v2 (the new lists). v2 names cash paid in (counter, deposit machine, Post Office and PayPoint wording) as cash_deposit, and names cash-withdrawal wording that only the cash round-trip indicator reads. Precedence: per-line override, then protected built-in patterns (returned DD, director, capital, shareholder, lender, HMRC), then profile names (directors, own accounts), then firm rules, then the rest of the built-in table, then the default (a debit is supplier, a credit is unexplained). Each line records which rule set its category. A pattern that is ambiguous between buckets resolves to one that needs judgement, never to trading receipts; cash wording is not ambiguous, and counting cash as trading is the owner's decision (D31).
91:- **C10 Synthetic data and evals** (src/cma/synth.py, evals/run_evals.py). New opt-in features, cash included, with truth for every bucket, line and indicator.
92:- **C11 Report** (CLI over C3). A local per-case summary with no personal data and no durations.
93:- **C12 Existing paths** (graph.py, cli.py, mcp_server.py, llm.py, policy.py). Behaviour unchanged; new fields are additive; the offline lock is checked. policy.evaluate and PolicyResult are reused as they are.
